  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(193.02pt, 567pt, ", one would expect two ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 578.523pt, "orders of magnitude smaller loss in a thermoelectric in ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 590.046pt, "comparison with a solar cell. ")
  #line-at(71.998pt, 613.032pt, "Considerable research activity exists to reduce or ")
  #line-at(71.988pt, 624.555pt, "eliminate this loss in “hot carrier solar cells” [23 -26]. ")
  #line-at(71.988pt, 636.078pt, "The thermodynamic view suggests that, by decoupling ")
  #line-at(71.988pt, 647.541pt, "carrier thermalization from photons, cooling of ")
  #line-at(71.988pt, 659.064pt, "carriers can be carried out adiabatically, in a similar ")
  #line-at(71.988pt, 670.587pt, "strategy to thermoelectric generators [16]. ")
  #line-at(71.988pt, 693.573pt, "Solar cells and thermoelectric generators are not, of ")
  #line-at(71.988pt, 705.036pt, "course, energy converters but power converters. The ")
  #line-at(323.991pt, 81.391pt, "effect of current generation on voltage can be ")
  #line-at(323.991pt, 92.854pt, "displayed by way of voltage-current characteristic, in ")
  #line-at(323.991pt, 104.377pt, "a form common in electrochemistry. The quasi-static ")
  #line-at(323.991pt, 115.9pt, "energy / voltage generation at open circuit can be ")
  #line-at(323.991pt, 127.362pt, "parallel the operation of a heat engine in classical ")
  #line-at(323.991pt, 138.885pt, "thermodynamics. With the passage of  fine current, ")
  #line-at(323.991pt, 150.408pt, "voltage will be reduced by entropy generation, as ")
  #line-at(323.991pt, 161.871pt, "predicted by finite-time (irreversible) thermodynamics ")
  #line-at(323.981pt, 173.394pt, "[5, 21, 22]. ")
  #line-at(323.981pt, 196.44pt, "The generated voltage can then be written as ")
