  #line-at(323.992pt, 349.137pt, "In thermoelectrics, this term would arise from a finite ")
  #line-at(323.992pt, 360.66pt, "rate (and therefore irreversible) of heat exchange ")
  #line-at(323.992pt, 372.123pt, "between the generator and the two thermal reservoirs. ")
  #line-at(323.992pt, 383.646pt, "If the loss (9) is neglected, the thermoelectric ")
  #line-at(323.992pt, 395.169pt, "generator becomes an endoreversible heat engine [6]. ")
  #line-at(324.002pt, 412.633pt, "The second term in brackets on the right hand side of ")
  #line-at(323.992pt, 424.156pt, "Eq. (19) is due to resistive losses in the two legs of the ")
  #line-at(323.992pt, 435.679pt, "thermoelectric generator,  or in the quasi-neutral ")
  #line-at(324.002pt, 447.142pt, "charge collection regions in solar cells. In solar cells, ")
  #line-at(324.002pt, 458.665pt, "the resistance")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(378.421pt, 458.665pt, " R")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.02pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(387.298pt, 458.665pt, " appears as the series resistance in the ")
  #line-at(323.992pt, 470.188pt, "current-voltage characteristic which, in good solar ")
  #line-at(323.982pt, 481.651pt, "cells, is small.  ")
  #line-at(323.972pt, 504.637pt, "In conclusion, we have shown that there is a ")
  #line-at(323.982pt, 516.16pt, "fundamental ")
  #line-at(385.665pt, 516.16pt, "similarity ")
  #line-at(435.648pt, 516.16pt, "between ")
  #line-at(480.651pt, 516.16pt, "energy/voltage ")
  #line-at(323.982pt, 527.683pt, "production in thermoelectric generators and solar cells ")
  #line-at(323.982pt, 539.146pt, "which, in standard devices, can be pictured as ")
  #line-at(323.982pt, 550.669pt, "isochoric chemical heat engines. The isochoric nature  ")
  #line-at(323.982pt, 562.192pt, "implies a thermalization loss by irreversibility which ")
  #line-at(323.982pt, 573.655pt, "is usually small in thermoelectrics but the main ")
  #line-at(323.982pt, 585.178pt, "efficiency loss in solar cells.  Extraction of current ")
  #line-at(323.982pt, 596.701pt, "moves the conversion process into the realm of finite-")
  #line-at(323.972pt, 608.164pt, "time irreversible thermodynamics. ")
